WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.989 --> 00:00:14.971
in a world with no magic?"

2
00:00:15.251 --> 00:00:16.032
Perda exclaimed.

3
00:00:16.052 --> 00:00:17.813
"You must be kidding!"

4
00:00:18.794 --> 00:00:19.495
"Not at all."

5
00:00:19.815 --> 00:00:20.356
said Wyssa.

6
00:00:20.876 --> 00:00:22.438
"Such places do exist."

7
00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:25.320
Feeling worried, Zann gulped.

8
00:00:26.121 --> 00:00:29.164
He and Perda had been unable to use their magic on other occasions.

9
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.541
Like when Morb was tracking them, or when they were in the Cave of the Unknown.

10
00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.342
But this situation was much worse.

11
00:00:37.342 --> 00:00:42.184
Zann felt completely helpless knowing that he couldn't use magic, even in an emergency.

12
00:00:42.204 --> 00:00:48.466
"This must be what it feels like to be a Void," Perda said, her voice shaking.

13
00:00:48.486 --> 00:00:53.707
"Or under a Dousing spell," Zann added, thinking briefly of Venna.

14
00:00:53.727 --> 00:00:56.508
"Don't get distracted," Wyssa ordered.

15
00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.961
"The signal that brought us here was strong and recent.

16
00:01:00.761 --> 00:01:03.342
If your friends are here, we need to find them quickly.

17
00:01:04.062 --> 00:01:07.023
And it won't be easy, since we can't use magic."

18
00:01:08.263 --> 00:01:09.584
Zann took a deep breath.

19
00:01:09.604 --> 00:01:15.165
"Okay. If they came through the same wormhole, they should still be nearby, right?

20
00:01:16.205 --> 00:01:18.806
After all, they wouldn't be able to zap anywhere else."

21
00:01:18.826 --> 00:01:20.867
"Good thinking, boy."

22
00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.007
Wyssa sounded almost impressed.

23
00:01:24.028 --> 00:01:29.121
"Speaking of the wormhole, I guess we can't use magic to find it again," Perda pointed out.

24
00:01:29.141 --> 00:01:32.542
"We'd better make sure we remember where it is."

25
00:01:33.682 --> 00:01:34.422
Zann nodded.

26
00:01:34.803 --> 00:01:37.363
The wormhole had closed as soon as they stepped away.

27
00:01:38.464 --> 00:01:39.584
But he remembered where it was.

28
00:01:40.024 --> 00:01:43.065
He stepped toward the spot, waiting for the wormhole to open again.

29
00:01:43.585 --> 00:01:44.325
But nothing happened.

30
00:01:44.345 --> 00:01:46.546
"Are you sure it was there?"

31
00:01:46.766 --> 00:01:47.326
Perda asked.

32
00:01:48.106 --> 00:01:49.967
"Maybe it was a little more to the left."

33
00:01:50.907 --> 00:01:52.207
Zann took a step to the left.

34
00:01:52.548 --> 00:01:53.868
The wormhole still didn't appear.

35
00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.322
"Use your heads, you two," Wyssa said harshly.

36
00:01:57.342 --> 00:02:00.264
"You need magic to open a wormhole.

37
00:02:00.344 --> 00:02:01.365
Everyone knows that!"

38
00:02:02.465 --> 00:02:06.088
She turned and hurried off, leaving Zann and Perda staring at each other.

39
00:02:06.108 --> 00:02:10.731
"But if there's no magic here—" Zann began.

40
00:02:11.732 --> 00:02:15.014
we have no way of opening the wormhole!"

41
00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:16.975
Perda swallowed hard.

42
00:02:16.995 --> 00:02:20.238
"So how are we ever supposed to leave this world?"

43
00:02:21.158 --> 00:02:23.320
Wyssa had almost disappeared into the crowds.

44
00:02:24.576 --> 00:02:27.477
"We'll have to worry about that later, I guess," Zann said.

45
00:02:27.497 --> 00:02:30.058
"First, let's find the others."

46
00:02:31.059 --> 00:02:33.620
He and Perda followed Wyssa, which wasn't easy.

47
00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:38.842
This world was much more crowded than anywhere in Magica, even First City.

48
00:02:39.603 --> 00:02:42.864
"How are we going to find our friends among all these people?"

49
00:02:43.744 --> 00:02:46.626
Perda wondered as she and Zann finally caught up with Wyssa.

50
00:02:47.406 --> 00:02:49.107
Wyssa stared around uncertainly.

51
00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:51.948
"I'm not sure," she admitted.

52
00:02:52.448 --> 00:02:54.630
"I suppose we'll just have to start looking."

53
00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:58.132
A toddler passed by, clinging to her mother's hand.

54
00:02:58.972 --> 00:03:02.255
The little girl babbled curiously, pointing at Zann's head.

55
00:03:02.275 --> 00:03:08.399
"I think she was staring at my hair," Zann said as the mother pulled the toddler away.

56
00:03:09.359 --> 00:03:11.381
Glancing around, he noticed something.

57
00:03:11.401 --> 00:03:15.363
"Look, almost everyone here has dark hair.

58
00:03:16.104 --> 00:03:18.686
That should make it easier to spot Darb and Gliss."

59
00:03:18.706 --> 00:03:20.727
"You're right!"

60
00:03:21.147 --> 00:03:21.888
Perda exclaimed.

61
00:03:22.316 --> 00:03:24.178
"Gliss has bright red hair like yours.

62
00:03:24.638 --> 00:03:25.619
And Darb's is light.

63
00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.521
Both of them should stand out in this crowd."

64
00:03:29.342 --> 00:03:30.363
Wyssa looked relieved.

65
00:03:30.823 --> 00:03:31.844
"Yes, that's true.

66
00:03:32.785 --> 00:03:36.388
Come, let's ask the natives if they've seen them."

67
00:03:36.428 --> 00:03:38.370
Zann stopped a man who was passing by.

68
00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:40.611
"Pardon me," Zann said.

69
00:03:40.631 --> 00:03:43.874
"Have you seen a girl around here with hair like mine?"

70
00:03:45.095 --> 00:03:46.977
The man paused and stared at Zann.

71
00:03:46.997 --> 00:03:49.018
"No, I'm sorry," he said.

72
00:03:49.038 --> 00:03:50.640
"Is she lost?

73
00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.781
Perhaps you should notify the police."

74
00:03:52.801 --> 00:03:54.462
"The police?"

75
00:03:54.883 --> 00:03:56.404
Perda said as the man moved on.

76
00:03:56.424 --> 00:03:57.585
"What's that?"

77
00:03:57.605 --> 00:04:00.426
"I have no idea," said Wyssa.

78
00:04:00.446 --> 00:04:01.827
"Let's check in here."

79
00:04:02.748 --> 00:04:04.389
She led the way into a marketplace.

80
00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:07.351
It was even more crowded than the street outside.

81
00:04:07.371 --> 00:04:10.914
"Look at all this stuff," Zann said.

82
00:04:10.934 --> 00:04:12.855
"Do you think it's food?"

83
00:04:12.875 --> 00:04:15.977
"Yes—look!" Perda pointed.

84
00:04:15.997 --> 00:04:18.299
"Here's a whole bin full of turnips.

85
00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:20.140
Teplo was right.

86
00:04:20.544 --> 00:04:22.486
They do come from another world!"

87
00:04:22.506 --> 00:04:30.272
"If turnips originally came from this world, that means somebody traveled from here to Magica," Zann said.

88
00:04:30.292 --> 00:04:34.395
"So there must be a way to open the wormhole without magic!"

89
00:04:34.415 --> 00:04:37.438
"True." Perda picked up a turnip.

90
00:04:37.458 --> 00:04:41.481
"How do you think the people here create their food without magic?"

91
00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:44.283
Just then a woman came over.

92
00:04:44.303 --> 00:04:45.805
"May I help you?"

93
00:04:46.165 --> 00:04:46.625
she asked.

94
00:04:46.645 --> 00:04:49.788
"We're looking for our friends," Zann said.

95
00:04:50.352 --> 00:04:53.954
"A red-haired girl, a light-haired boy, and a small dragon."

96
00:04:53.974 --> 00:04:57.717
"A dragon, huh?"

97
00:04:58.017 --> 00:05:01.259
The woman laughed, even though Zann hadn't said anything funny.

98
00:05:01.279 --> 00:05:05.141
"The only dragon I've seen lately is right over there."

99
00:05:06.061 --> 00:05:09.403
She pointed at a banner with a picture of a fierce golden dragon on it.

100
00:05:09.423 --> 00:05:13.746
"No, Zing is much smaller, and—" Zann began.

101
00:05:14.486 --> 00:05:16.788
But the woman was already talking to another customer.

102
00:05:17.916 --> 00:05:23.100
After that Zann, Perda, and Wyssa asked more people if they'd seen Darb, Gliss, or Zing.

103
00:05:24.021 --> 00:05:30.005
However, as soon as Zann described Zing, people either laughed at him or got angry and hurried off.

104
00:05:31.066 --> 00:05:31.986
"I'm serious!"

105
00:05:32.327 --> 00:05:35.469
Zann insisted as yet another woman chuckled and shook her head.

106
00:05:35.489 --> 00:05:41.833
"He's about this big, with reddish-colored scales "Very funny, young man."

107
00:05:42.114 --> 00:05:42.954
The woman smiled.

108
00:05:43.675 --> 00:05:45.236
"Excuse me, I'm late for work."

109
00:05:46.492 --> 00:05:49.393
As the woman hurried off, Perda sighed with frustration.

110
00:05:49.413 --> 00:05:51.634
"This place is weird.

111
00:05:52.094 --> 00:05:54.934
It's like nobody here has ever seen a real dragon before!"

112
00:05:55.195 --> 00:05:55.835
she exclaimed.

113
00:05:56.755 --> 00:05:58.415
Zann felt a tap on his shoulder.

114
00:05:58.916 --> 00:06:00.816
Turning, he saw a young man.

115
00:06:00.836 --> 00:06:03.257
"Excuse me," the man said.

116
00:06:03.277 --> 00:06:04.917
"You're looking for a dragon?

117
00:06:05.737 --> 00:06:06.658
A real one?"

118
00:06:06.678 --> 00:06:09.539
"Yes!" Zann suddenly felt hopeful.

119
00:06:10.019 --> 00:06:10.939
"His name is Zing.

120
00:06:11.199 --> 00:06:11.939
Have you seen him?"

121
00:06:12.759 --> 00:06:14.400
The man indicated for them to follow.

122
00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:19.243
He led the way out of the market, across the street, and into a shop.

123
00:06:20.223 --> 00:06:24.967
The shop was crammed with knick-knacks, including a whole shelf full of fake dragons.

124
00:06:25.927 --> 00:06:29.330
For a moment Zann was afraid that the man had misunderstood him.

125
00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:34.333
"This way," the young man said, stepping into a dimly lit back room.

126
00:06:35.314 --> 00:06:36.735
Zann entered and gasped.

127
00:06:36.755 --> 00:06:42.839
"Zing!" he cried, spotting his dragon cowering behind the bars of a small metal cage.
